  'ups-sizing': {"title":"UPS Battery Sizing Calculator: Load, Backup Time","metaDesc":"UPS Battery Sizing Calculator computes a battery capacity of 29.4 Ah from your load and backup time and shows each step of the calculation.","canonicalPath":"/engineering/ups-sizing","cat":"engineering","catName":"Engineering","lsi":["ups battery sizing calculator ah runtime backup load inverter","free online ups battery sizing calculator","ups battery sizing formula","how to calculate ups battery","battery capacity formula"],"aeo":"<h2>What does this calculator do?</h2>\n<p>UPS Battery Sizing Calculator works out the battery capacity from the Load, Backup Time, and Battery Bank Voltage, following standard Engineering conventions — the page defaults produce a battery capacity of 29.4 Ah.</p><ul><li><strong>Inputs:</strong> Load, Backup Time, and Battery Bank Voltage.</li><li><strong>Output:</strong> the battery capacity, plus the intermediate steps behind it.</li><li><strong>Method:</strong> standard Engineering arithmetic for the battery capacity, computed on the device.</li></ul><h3>Quick answer</h3>\n<p>With the default inputs (load of 600, backup time of 30, battery bank voltage of 12), ups battery sizing calculator returns a battery capacity of 29.4 Ah.</p><h2>How does it work?</h2>\n<p>UPS Battery Sizing Calculator computes the battery capacity directly from your inputs — the Load, Backup Time, and Battery Bank Voltage feed the formula. The battery capacity is derived locally, which is why the page still works after the connection drops.</p>","desc":"<h2>How the UPS Battery Sizing Calculator works</h2>\n<p>UPS Battery Sizing Calculator answers one question well — given the values you provide, what is the battery capacity? Enter the Load, Backup Time, and Battery Bank Voltage, and the result panel returns the value with the full working underneath.</p>\n<h2>How to use it</h2>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Load</strong> — one of the values the calculation builds from; the result reflects exactly what you type here.</li>\n<li><strong>Backup Time</strong> — used in the first stage of the calculation, so entering it accurately matters more than any later refinement.</li>\n<li><strong>Battery Bank Voltage</strong> — the value that feeds directly into the formula — match it to the scenario you are modeling before moving on.</li>\n<li>Note the output UPS Battery Sizing Calculator reports. It updates as you type, and the worked steps beneath UPS Battery Sizing Calculator make the arithmetic auditable.</li>\n<li>Adjust and re-run. Change one input at a time to see how sensitive the battery capacity is to it — the fastest way to understand what the calculation is doing.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>The formula behind the result</h2>\n<p>The relationship between the inputs is fixed by the formula, and UPS Battery Sizing Calculator makes each substitution explicit so nothing about the battery capacity is hidden.</p>\n<p><strong>Worked example:</strong> with load of 600, backup time of 30, battery bank voltage of 12, this ups battery sizing calculation returns <strong>Battery Capacity: 29.4 Ah</strong>. The same run reports Energy needed: 0.30 kWh | Add about 25% margin for aging and cold → 36.8 Ah.</p><p>The steps it follows:</p><ul><li>Formula: Ah = (load × hours) ÷ (V × efficiency)</li><li>Energy = 600 W × 0.50 h = 300 Wh</li><li>Delivered from batteries = Wh ÷ 12 V ÷ 0.85 = 29.4 Ah</li><li>Lead-acid rated at the 20-hour rate delivers less at high draw — check the discharge curve for short runtimes</li></ul>\n<h2>Understanding the result</h2>\n<p>To interpret the result from ups battery sizing calculator, read it together with the intermediate figures — the pairing is what makes the number auditable.</p>\n<h2>Where it helps</h2>\n<p>UPS Battery Sizing Calculator fits planning and checking: planning ahead, weighing two choices, and spot-checking a quoted figure, or any moment when the output needs to be right the first time.</p>\n<h2>Common mistakes</h2>\n<p>Mixing up inputs with similar labels is the classic ups battery sizing mistake; the steps panel is the quickest way to spot a value that landed in the wrong field.</p>\n<p><strong>Tip:</strong> UPS Battery Sizing Calculator returns Battery Capacity: 29.4 Ah at its defaults; double the Load (W) and it returns Battery Capacity: 58.8 Ah.</p>\n<h2>Assumptions and limitations</h2>\n<p>The assumptions listed for ups battery sizing calculator bound the estimate: inputs outside the labeled ranges can make the battery capacity mathematically valid but practically implausible.</p>\n<h2>Why use this calculator</h2>\n<p>Because the page doubles as documentation: UPS Battery Sizing Calculator puts the formula, a worked example, and the assumptions right beside the calculator.</p>","faqs":[{"q":"What does this calculator do?","a":"UPS Battery Sizing Calculator is built for ups battery sizing questions that need a defensible number: the working is always visible, the inputs accept your own values, and the figure updates as you type. Choosing ups battery sizing calculator comes down to transparency — the working stays visible, the math stays local, and the result is reproducible line by line."},{"q":"How is the battery capacity calculated?","a":"The first steps are formula: ah = (load × hours) ÷ (v × efficiency), then energy = 600 w × 0.50 h = 300 wh. The formula section on this page spells out how ups battery sizing calculator turns the Load, Backup Time, and Battery Bank Voltage into the battery capacity, one operation at a time."},{"q":"What do I need to use the UPS Battery Sizing Calculator?","a":"UPS Battery Sizing Calculator needs Load, Backup Time, and Battery Bank Voltage and nothing else."},{"q":"What happens if I double the Load (W)?","a":"At the defaults UPS Battery Sizing Calculator returns Battery Capacity: 29.4 Ah; doubling Load (W) to 1,200 moves it to Battery Capacity: 58.8 Ah."},{"q":"What does the result from this calculator mean?","a":"The main number the ups battery sizing calculator returns is the battery capacity for your exact inputs. The model behind UPS Battery Sizing Calculator covers the standard case; special cases, edge values, or jurisdiction-specific rules may need manual adjustment."},{"q":"When is the page most useful?","a":"Typical uses for UPS Battery Sizing Calculator include planning ahead, weighing two choices, and spot-checking a quoted figure — anywhere the figure needs to be defensible rather than guessed. A useful habit with ups battery sizing calculator: vary one input at a time and note how far the battery capacity moves before trusting any single run."}]},
