  'payday-loan-cost': {"title":"Payday Loan Cost Calculator: Loan Amount, Fee per $100","metaDesc":"Payday Loan Cost Calculator computes an apr of 391.1% from your loan amount and fee per $100 and shows each step of the calculation.","canonicalPath":"/finance/payday-loan-cost","cat":"finance","catName":"Finance","lsi":["payday loan cost calculator true cost","free online payday loan cost calculator","payday loan cost formula","how to calculate payday loan","apr formula"],"aeo":"<h2>What does the Payday Loan Cost Calculator do?</h2>\n<p>Payday Loan Cost Calculator works out the apr from the Loan Amount, Fee per $100, and Days Until Payday, following standard Finance conventions — the page defaults produce an apr of 391.1%.</p><ul><li><strong>Inputs:</strong> Loan Amount, Fee per $100, and Days Until Payday.</li><li><strong>Output:</strong> the apr, plus the intermediate steps behind it.</li><li><strong>Method:</strong> the standard Finance method for the apr, run locally in your browser.</li></ul><h3>Quick answer</h3>\n<p>With the default inputs (loan amount of 500, fee per $100 of 15, days until payday of 14), payday loan cost calculator returns an apr of 391.1%.</p><h2>How does the Payday Loan Cost Calculator work?</h2>\n<p>Payday Loan Cost Calculator computes the apr directly from your inputs — the Loan Amount, Fee per $100, and Days Until Payday feed the formula. The apr is calculated in the browser, so the inputs never leave the device.</p>","desc":"<h2>How it works</h2>\n<p>This page is a working payday loan cost calculator: enter your values, read the output, and follow the step list to see exactly how the answer was derived.</p>\n<h2>Using the Payday Loan Cost Calculator</h2>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Loan Amount</strong> — in payday loan cost calculator, this value feeds the formula directly, and the steps panel shows exactly where it enters the apr.</li>\n<li><strong>Fee per $100</strong> — used in the first stage of the calculation, so entering it accurately matters more than any later refinement.</li>\n<li><strong>Days Until Payday</strong> — the value that feeds directly into the formula — match it to the scenario you are modeling before moving on.</li>\n<li>The output panel in payday loan cost calculator leads with the headline result and follows with the steps behind it, so the value can be checked rather than assumed.</li>\n<li>When rerunning payday loan cost calculator, change a single input between attempts — the resulting spread shows which factor actually drives the apr.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>The formula behind the result</h2>\n<p>Rounding follows standard display conventions — the underlying math keeps several decimal places until the apr is shown.</p>\n<p><strong>Worked example:</strong> with loan amount of 500, fee per $100 of 15, days until payday of 14, this payday loan cost calculation returns <strong>APR: 391.1%</strong>. The same run reports Total repayment: $575.00 | Fee: $75.00.</p><p>The steps it follows:</p><ul><li>Fee = ($500 / $100) × $15 = $75.00</li><li>APR = (Fee / Principal) × (365 / Days) × 100</li><li>= ($75.00 / $500) × (365 / 14) × 100</li><li>APR = 391.1%</li></ul>\n<h2>Understanding the result</h2>\n<p>To interpret the result from payday loan cost calculator, read it together with the intermediate figures — the pairing is what makes the number auditable.</p>\n<h2>Where it helps</h2>\n<p>Payday Loan Cost Calculator fits planning and checking: day-to-day planning, weighing two choices, and double-checking a figure before acting on it, or any moment when the figure needs to be right the first time.</p>\n<h2>Common mistakes</h2>\n<p>Rounding intermediate values by hand introduces error Payday Loan Cost Calculator does not have; it keeps full precision internally, so trust the displayed apr over mental arithmetic.</p>\n<p><strong>Tip:</strong> Payday Loan Cost Calculator returns APR: 391.1% at its defaults; double the Loan Amount ($) and it returns APR: 391.1%.</p>\n<h2>Assumptions and limitations</h2>\n<p>The assumptions listed for payday loan cost calculator bound the estimate: inputs outside the labeled ranges can make the apr mathematically valid but practically implausible.</p>\n<h2>Why use this calculator</h2>\n<p>Choosing payday loan cost calculator comes down to transparency — the working stays visible, the math stays local, and the result is reproducible line by line.</p>","faqs":[{"q":"What does the Payday Loan Cost Calculator calculate?","a":"Payday Loan Cost Calculator keeps the whole calculation in front of you — the Loan Amount, Fee per $100, and Days Until Payday, the formula, the intermediate steps, and a worked example you can reproduce line by line. Because the page doubles as documentation: Payday Loan Cost Calculator puts the formula, a worked example, and the assumptions right beside the calculator."},{"q":"How is the apr calculated?","a":"The first steps are fee = ($500 / $100) × $15 = $75.00, then apr = (fee / principal) × (365 / days) × 100. The calculation in Payday Loan Cost Calculator applies the standard Finance method, keeping full precision internally and rounding only the final display."},{"q":"What do I need to use the Payday Loan Cost Calculator?","a":"Payday Loan Cost Calculator needs Loan Amount, Fee per $100, and Days Until Payday and nothing else."},{"q":"What happens if I double the Loan Amount ($)?","a":"At the defaults Payday Loan Cost Calculator returns APR: 391.1%; doubling Loan Amount ($) to 1,000 moves it to APR: 391.1%."},{"q":"What does the result from the Payday Loan Cost Calculator mean?","a":"The main number the payday loan cost calculator returns is the apr for your exact inputs. In practice, the assumptions listed for payday loan cost calculator bound the estimate: inputs outside the labeled ranges can make the apr mathematically valid but practically implausible."},{"q":"When is the Payday Loan Cost Calculator most useful?","a":"Typical uses for Payday Loan Cost Calculator include day-to-day planning, weighing two choices, and double-checking a figure before acting on it — anywhere the figure needs to be defensible rather than guessed. In practice, a useful habit with payday loan cost calculator: vary one input at a time and note how far the apr moves before trusting any single run."}]},
